1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:07,241
A mapping tells software developers where an information unit is stored in a data format that tools already support.

2
00:00:08,141 --> 00:00:13,643
Each information unit can have one or more corresponding external elements.

3
00:00:13,643 --> 00:00:18,999
Built-in schemas include bSDD, IFC and CityGML, and you can add your own.

4
00:00:19,899 --> 00:00:24,401
Open the defect inspection form, expand Location, and select Storey.

5
00:00:25,749 --> 00:00:31,036
Click Add Mapping, choose IFC 4x3 ADD2, and search for IfcBuildingStorey.

6
00:00:31,036 --> 00:00:37,120
The search lists the attributes the entity defines itself; pick one and click Apply.

7
00:00:39,649 --> 00:00:45,968
The storey name is inherited from IfcRoot, so edit the path directly: IfcBuildingStorey dot Name.

8
00:00:45,968 --> 00:00:49,420
The path is free text; search only helps you find it.

9
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:59,249
BCF, the BIM Collaboration Format of buildingSMART, exchanges issues as topics, with viewpoints that point to model elements.

10
00:00:59,249 --> 00:01:04,677
It is a natural format for defects, so we map the defect information to BCF.

11
00:01:05,577 --> 00:01:09,375
Open the defect log entry, expand Defect, and select Title.

12
00:01:11,427 --> 00:01:13,548
BCF 3.0 is not built in.

13
00:01:13,548 --> 00:01:18,760
Click Add Mapping, and in the basis list choose Add schema.

14
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:25,827
Start from the BCF 3.0 preset, with its 120 element paths, and click Add schema.

15
00:01:26,727 --> 00:01:32,146
Now search the BCF elements for Title, and apply Markup slash Topic slash Title.

16
00:01:36,427 --> 00:01:41,742
The catch-up file DMBCF_5e_mappings.idm has all 64 mappings.

17
00:01:41,742 --> 00:01:45,729
Close the project without saving and open it.

18
00:01:46,629 --> 00:01:53,974
Information that BCF does not define, such as severity, travels as a label from the project extensions file.

19
00:01:53,974 --> 00:01:56,762
Some information is not exchanged at all.

